            <p>
                <strong>7. </strong>
                This question has two parts. Answer Part A and then Part B.
            </p>
            <p>
                <strong>Part A </strong>
                How is &quot;Lost in the Dust&quot; different from &quot;A Long Drought&quot;?
            </p>
            <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_1" shuffle="false" max-choices="1" min-choices="1">
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic001">
                    <strong>A. </strong>
                    It gives a lot of facts and information about dust storms.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic002">
                    <strong>B. </strong>
                    It describes how the area was affected by a long drought.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic003">
                    <strong>C. </strong>
                    It was written by someone who experienced the events.
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic004">
                    <strong>D. </strong>
                    It mentions the idea of moving to California to find work.
                </qti-simple-choice>
            </qti-choice-interaction>
            <p>
                <strong>Part B </strong>
                Which sentence from the passage supports the answer to Part A?
            </p>
            <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE_2" shuffle="false" max-choices="1" min-choices="1">
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic005">
                    <strong>A. </strong>
                    &quot;If a storm approached while I was at school, Mama would rush over in the car to drive me home while Daddy scrambled to get the cows into the barn.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic006">
                    <strong>B. </strong>
                    &quot;Even on calm days, the dust hung in the air.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic007">
                    <strong>C. </strong>
                    &quot;Instead it just scooped up the dust piles and threw them somewhere else.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
                <qti-simple-choice identifier="X91137-t01as01asi007asic008">
                    <strong>D. </strong>
                    &quot;As it turned out, the droughts dragged on five more years.&quot;
                </qti-simple-choice>
            </qti-choice-interaction>
        </div>
